From 8a9daa146a8fafa977a6e9266beff574d11e4497 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:36:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 28/52] Security hardening: public allowlist, /tag shared
 secret, source binding, expiry, rate limits, masking

- SecurityGuardMiddleware (Security.AccessMode): PublicMatchmaker answers
  only /match, /mms and /tag from the internet (WebUI and card APIs are
  loopback-only, 403); LanOnly card servers answer loopback/private
  networks only (ExtraAllowedCidrs to widen).
- /tag requires the X-Tag-Secret header (OnlineTag.TagSecret, never in
  the repo; deploy.sh --tag-secret-file); 401 without it.
- Per-IP token-bucket rate limits: /match 1200/min burst 300, /tag
  240/min burst 60 (429).
- Matchmaker.BindNodesToSource: CheckMatching/CancelMatching from a
  different source than the node's EntryMatching are refused (SRC-WARN).
- TagInviteStore.RegisterSearch keeps only codes the pilot created or
  joined; open codes expire after 7 days, joined codes after 90.
- Logs mask public IPv4 (a.b.x.x) and partner codes (AB******).
- WebUI card list no longer returns chip ids (masked hint ****1234);
  authorize returns the chip id only after the access code matched.
- tools/vps: apply-security-config.py, UMask=0077, server.json 0640.
229 unit tests pass.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
