diff --git a/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md b/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
index a045fd7..25c0e1a 100644
--- a/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
+++ b/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
@@ -256,6 +256,53 @@ exvs2-lobbies `server-sketch/loadtest/hangfix_e2e.py`.
   (ms) is the RTT above which hole punching fails with "RTT out of limit"; `ThresholdDelayedFrame` the input-delay
   frames above which a match counts as delayed. Same values on every server of a group.
 
+## Security hardening (2026-11-15)
+
+Config: `CardServerConfig.Security` and `CardServerConfig.OnlineTag` in `Configurations/server.json`.
+
+- **Who can connect** (`Security.AccessMode`). Middleware runs before the WebUI, static files and every controller.
+  It uses the real connection address and never trusts `X-Forwarded-For`.
+  - `LanOnly` is the default, for a card server. Every path answers only loopback, 10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16,
+    169.254/16, ::1, fc00::/7 and fe80::/10, plus `ExtraAllowedCidrs` (for example `100.64.0.0/10` for Tailscale or
+    `26.0.0.0/8` for Radmin). Other sources get 403 with no body. Nothing changes in Windows Firewall or TinyWall.
+  - `PublicMatchmaker` is for the VPS. The internet can reach only `/match`, `/mms` and `/tag`. The WebUI, `/ui`,
+    `/sys`, `/game`, uploads, swagger and static files answer loopback only, so use an SSH tunnel for admin.
+  - `Open` is the upstream behaviour. Not recommended.
+- **`/tag` shared secret** (`OnlineTag.TagSecret`, header `X-Tag-Secret`). The matchmaker and every card server that
+  uses it must have the same value. Every `/tag` call without it gets 401, including
+  `GET /tag/invites/{code}` and `GET /tag/invites/for/{pilotId}`, and LAN callers need it too. With no secret set,
+  `/tag` answers LAN sources only. Keep the secret out of git: put it in the local `server.json` (restrict the file's
+  permissions) or the environment variable `CardServerConfig__OnlineTag__TagSecret`. The startup config dump leaves
+  it out. `/tag/register` keeps only codes that the given pilot created or joined.
+- **`/match` hardening.** Cabinets call `/match` directly and send no secret, so `/match` stays public but is
+  hardened. With `Security.BindMatchNodesToSourceIp` (default on), CheckMatching and CancelMatching for a node are
+  honoured only from the source IP that sent that node's EntryMatching. A stranger who guesses node ids gets
+  `ERR_MATCH_NOENTRY` and cannot read the room roster (peer IPs), and their cancel is ignored and logged as
+  `SRC-WARN`. Cabinets behind one NAT share an IP, so this is safe for shops and homes. Replies are unchanged
+  otherwise: the game needs the room's client list to connect.
+- **Rate limits.** Each source IP gets a token bucket. `/match` and `/mms` allow 1200 requests per minute with a
+  burst of 300; a cabinet polls about every 3 s, so 16 or more cabinets behind one IP never hit it. `/tag` allows
+  240 per minute with a burst of 60. Over the limit, the reply is 429 with `Retry-After: 5`. Loopback is exempt
+  unless `ExemptLoopbackFromRateLimit` is false.
+- **Partner codes expire.** An unjoined code expires after `OnlineTag.OpenCodeExpiryDays` (default 7) since it was
+  created or last shown with "Create a code"; LoadCard does not keep it alive. A joined team code expires after
+  `JoinedCodeExpiryDays` (default 90) with no LoadCard, Teams tab or settings save from either partner. 0 means
+  never. Expired codes and their world-5 registrations are removed from `tag_invites.json`. New codes come from a
+  CSPRNG.
+- **Logs** (`Security.MaskNetworkInLog`, default on). Every log property is masked: public IPv4 becomes `a.b.x.x`
+  and partner codes become `AB******`. That covers matchmaker lines, the "Request is" dump and request paths.
+  Private and loopback IPs are kept for LAN diagnostics.
+- **WebUI card list.** `/ui/card/getAll` no longer returns chip ids, only `chipIdHint` (`********1234`). The access
+  code dialog sends the card id and access code to `/ui/card/authorize`, which returns the chip id only when the code
+  matches (constant-time compare). Customize, View and the Teams tab then work as before. Search matches player names
+  partially but chip ids only in full, so it cannot be used to recover chip ids.
+- **VPS.** `tools/vps/deploy.sh` keeps `tag_invites.json` and `tag_server_id.txt` and backs up `tag_invites.json`
+  before each upload. It sets `AccessMode=PublicMatchmaker` if missing, takes `--tag-secret-file` (sent over SSH
+  stdin, never printed), and makes `server.json` mode 0640 root:exvs2mm. The service runs with `UMask=0077`.
+- Tests: `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/SecurityTests.cs`. `cross_server_tag_e2e.py` (exvs2-lobbies) runs the
+  cross-server pair with a per-run secret and also checks the 401s, the card list without chip ids, the authorize
+  flow, the `/tag` 429s and that logs contain no code, secret or public IP.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
 * Malformed protobuf bodies on `/match` get HTTP 500 from the model binder (the real cabinet never sends them).
