- WebUI saves the access code together with its chip id (one card at a
  time); pages re-check a saved login via POST ui/card/authorize (CardId 0
  + chip id) and ask to log in again instead of sending one card's access
  code with another card's chip id (500 "Card Profile is invalid").
- LogMask.MaskUrlSecrets + CardSecretMaskEnricher: access codes, chip ids
  and tokens in WebUI request paths (/ui/.../{accessCode}/{chipId},
  getBy/{accessCode}), token segments and secret query parameters become
  <masked:N> in every sink (request log, HttpClient log, errors).
- Matchmaker: a world-5 search that waits PartnerWaitLogAfter (20 s) logs
  once "TAG-WAIT node=N am=X waiting for partner <wire id>: partner not
  searching" (or that the partner is queued in another mode and cannot
  pair). Logging only.
- Tests: same-server code team still pairs, two tag pairs (cross-server
  and same-server) form one 2v2, TAG-WAIT once per search, path masking.
251 unit tests, cross_server_tag_e2e 53/53. Real game 2026-11-15
7:33 AM PT: 4 cabinets, two online-tag pairs, several 2v2 games completed.

