From 524090dfdf01297d5e25e847bc7d896d8e565168 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:09:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/52] Online tag: renames reach the partner's server,
 cross-server team delete, last-team delete

Renames: every tag-team sync (LoadCard / card insert and the WebUI Teams
tab) first reports the card's current player name to the matchmaker
(POST /tag/names {pilotId, name}); the store updates creatorName /
partnerName in every invite of that pilot. Names are trimmed, control /
format characters dropped, cut to 32 characters; >64 characters is a
400. A failed name report is logged and does not stop the sync.

Team delete: POST /tag/invites/{code}/delete {pilotId} lets either
partner remove a code; the invite and every codesByAm registration of
it are dropped, so the next sync cannot re-create the team. Unknown
codes answer deleted=false (retry-safe); a non-partner gets 400. The
WebUI save deletes a cross-server team on the matchmaker first and
keeps it locally (Success=false) if the matchmaker refuses or is
unreachable, instead of letting it come back on the next card insert.
Old matchmakers (404/405) get a readable "needs the update" message.

Last-team delete: an empty Teams list used to be ignored, so deleting
a card's last team did nothing. UpsertTeamsRequest gains DeletedTeamIds
(filled by the delete dialog); an empty list with deleted ids deletes
exactly those, an empty list without them still changes nothing.

/tag stays behind X-Tag-Secret and the /tag rate limit (new paths are
under /tag, allowlist unchanged). Codes stay masked in logs.
