From 9f064ba30f2f246ab6fee2d79a16ad510062ba4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:27:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 31/52] Friends: results-screen friend requests, block (NG)
 lists, Friends page

RegisterOption (306) is now always answered (empty success) when
Friends.Enabled (default true), independent of PostMatchStubs. Live
capture 2026-11-15 10:52 PT: mobile_user_id = sender's wire pilot id,
friend_pilot_id = partner's wire pilot id (other card server), ng = 0;
only the requester sends it. The card server forwards it in the
background to the matchmaker's /tag/friends API (same base URL,
X-Tag-Secret and rate limit as /tag; allowlist unchanged). If the
matchmaker is unreachable or too old, the request is kept in
friends_outbox.json and retried on the next 306 / card insert.

Matchmaker FriendStore (friends.json, atomic writes): A -> B is
pending; it becomes a friendship when B also asks or accepts on the
web. A new friendship ensures one joined online tag team for the pair
(TagInviteStore.EnsureJoinedPair, reused if one exists;
Friends.AutoCreateTagTeam). Block drops friendship / requests, refuses
requests both ways (RefusedBlocked / RefusedYouBlocked). Remove and
block never delete tag teams unless deleteTagTeams is set. Limits:
500 friends, 500 blocks, 100 sent / 200 received; pending expires after
30 days. /tag/names also updates friend names. Lists are searched
(name, case/width/kana-insensitive, or pilot-id digits), sorted
(name / added / lastPlayed) and paged (<= 100) on the matchmaker.

LoadCard: partner_recruit_am_id_nglist (25) = block list (newest
first, max 100, 2.5 s timeout then cached list). The cabinet copies it
into EntryMatching.bl_banapassport_am_ids, which the matchmaker honours.

WebUI: card menu -> Friends (/Cards/Friends/{chipId}): tabs Friends /
Requests (all, received, sent) / Blocked with counts, search, sort,
server-side paging (10/25/50/100), per-page bulk select with bulk
accept / decline / remove / block / unblock, confirm dialogs (with an
explicit "also delete our online tag teams" option), add by pilot id,
stacked rows on phones. Card secrets only in POST bodies. en + ja text.

deploy.sh never uploads / deletes friends.json(_outbox) and backs up
friends.json before each upload.

Tests: unit 293/293 (+30: FriendStoreTests, FriendOutboxTests,
TagPairTests); cross_server_tag_e2e 94/94 (53 existing + 41 friends).

