diff --git a/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md b/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
index 19033c0..916ef2f 100644
--- a/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
+++ b/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
@@ -311,6 +311,53 @@ Config: `CardServerConfig.Security` and `CardServerConfig.OnlineTag` in `Configu
   cross-server pair with a per-run secret and also checks the 401s, the card list without chip ids, the authorize
   flow, the `/tag` 429s and that logs contain no code, secret or public IP.
 
+## Friends and block lists (2026-11-15) — fake cabinets + one live capture
+
+**What the game sends.** Results screen → hold Start → フレンド申請 (friend request) or NG sends RegisterOption (306)
+from the requester's cabinet only: `mobile_user_id` = sender's wire pilot id, `friend_pilot_id` = partner's wire pilot
+id (may be on another card server), `ng_pilot_id` = a player to block. Live capture 2026-11-15 10:52 PT:
+`{1000002, 2000002, 0}`; the partner's cabinet sent nothing. The reply body is empty; only `Error = Success` matters.
+
+**Card server.** With `CardServerConfig.Friends.Enabled` (default true) 306 always gets the empty success reply
+(no longer depends on `PostMatchStubs`). The request is then forwarded in the background to the matchmaker's
+`/tag/friends` API (same URL base, `X-Tag-Secret` and rate limit as `/tag`, so no new port or allowlist entry).
+If the matchmaker is down or still on an older build, the request is kept in `friends_outbox.json` and retried on
+the next RegisterOption / card insert (dropped after 7 days). Senders that are not a card on this server are ignored.
+
+**Matchmaker (`friends.json`, atomic writes, backed up by `deploy.sh`).**
+* A → B is a pending request. It becomes a friendship when B also asks (game or web) or B accepts on the Friends page.
+* On a new friendship the matchmaker makes sure the two share a **joined online tag team** (reuses an existing one;
+  `Friends.AutoCreateTagTeam`). Card servers pick it up on the next card insert / Teams tab (the Friends page syncs at once).
+* Block: drops any friendship or request between the two; the blocked player gets `RefusedBlocked`, the blocker must
+  unblock before asking (`RefusedYouBlocked`). Remove / block **never** delete online tag teams unless the player ticks
+  "Also delete our online tag teams" (`deleteTagTeams`); then the codes are deleted on the matchmaker and the local rows
+  on this card server. (The partner's card server keeps a stale row until it is deleted there; it can no longer match.)
+* Limits per player: 500 friends, 500 blocks, 100 sent / 200 received requests; unanswered requests expire after 30 days.
+* Names come from the sender and from every `/tag/names` report (card insert / Teams tab).
+
+**LoadCard.** `MobileUserGroup.partner_recruit_am_id_nglist` (25) = the card's block list (newest first, max
+`Friends.MaxNgListEntries` = 100; `Friends.SendNgList`). The cabinet copies it into
+`EntryMatching.bl_banapassport_am_ids`, which the matchmaker already honours. Waits at most `LoadCardTimeoutMs`
+(2.5 s), then uses the last list seen. The game has no friend-list field in LoadCard (only counts in
+SaveUserPlayResearchData), so friendships are shown on the web page and as online tag teams in game.
+
+**API (matchmaker, header `X-Tag-Secret`).**
+`POST /tag/friends/request {fromPilotId, fromName, toPilotId, source}`;
+`POST /tag/friends/{accept|decline|remove|block|unblock} {pilotId, name, others[≤100], deleteTagTeams, source}`;
+`GET /tag/friends/{pilotId}?tab=friends|incoming|outgoing|requests|blocked&q=&sort=name|added|lastPlayed&dir=asc|desc&page=1&pageSize=25`
+(page size ≤ 100; search = name, case / width / kana insensitive, or pilot-id digits);
+`GET /tag/friends/{pilotId}/blocked?max=100`.
+Card-server WebUI: `POST /ui/friends/{list|request|blockId|accept|decline|remove|block|unblock}` with the card's
+access code + chip id in the body (never in the URL). Page: card menu → **Friends** (`/Cards/Friends/{chipId}`):
+tabs Friends / Requests (all, received, sent) / Blocked with counts, search, sort, server-side paging (10/25/50/100),
+per-page bulk select, confirm dialogs, add by pilot id. Works at phone widths (rows stack).
+
+**Tests.** `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests`: FriendStoreTests, FriendOutboxTests (RegisterOption logic + outbox),
+TagPairTests. `server-sketch/loadtest/cross_server_tag_e2e.py` section 4b (41 checks): A-server card requests a
+B-server card from the results screen → pending → accepted on the web → both friends + one joined online tag team in
+the Teams tab and LoadCard; mutual game requests; block / NG / unblock with LoadCard field 25; remove with team
+delete; bulk 30 + paging / search / page-size cap; `/tag/friends` behind the secret.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
 * Malformed protobuf bodies on `/match` get HTTP 500 from the model binder (the real cabinet never sends them).
