From 2c809f5cbf96e608b527f99d0f157cc52b447141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:50:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 32/52] Friends: last played from real match results; WebUI
 survives a dropped startup fetch

Last played: when a card server saves a versus result (SaveVsmOnResult
online, SaveVsmResult in-store), the result's partner + foes pilot ids
(CPU slots skipped, max 8) go in the background to the matchmaker's new
POST /tag/friends/played (X-Tag-Secret like the rest of /tag). The
FriendStore stamps last played on every friendship / pending request
between that player and them, teammates and opponents, across card
servers; never moves backwards; best effort (one try, failure logged).
Friends.TrackLastPlayed (default true). The matchmaker room list was not
used: it only sees a room form, not a battle finish.

WebUI: the browser sometimes cancels the first data fetch of a cold page
load (data/Bgms.json, net::ERR_ABORTED before reaching the server; also
on the base build, 1 in 3-8 headless loads). Startup awaits that data,
so any page stayed on "Loading..." with "An unhandled error has
occurred" (the blank menu / phone screenshots). The client HttpClient
now retries GET / HEAD that failed without a response (200/600/1500 ms;
POSTs never repeated). Verified: 0 of 10 cold loads fail, one dropped
fetch recovered.

Tests: unit 300/300 (+7 FriendPlayedTests); cross_server_tag_e2e
103/103 (+9 last-played checks).

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
