From 6861fc064982525703839d0bbd7ac9c466abcf8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:57:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/52] Matchmaker: continue-pair fix (VsCpu, 18 s) and fast
 cancel for CPU-partner entries under NoCpuPartner

4-cab tests 12:45 / 13:19 / 13:49 PT: two idle teammates are auto-continued by the game as a pair after the
results screen. With NoCpuPartner that pair was held for a 4-human room, the leader's cabinet cancelled itself at
~30 s (CheckCommunication found_player=false, UdpHp 1), both cabinets showed the "partner connection lost" popup
and went black waiting on each other.

- ContinuePairMode (Off / Cancel / VsCpu) + ContinuePairSeconds: a pair whose nodes were on the same side of a
  recent room gets a lone-team-vs-CPU room (VsCpu, no human gets a CPU partner) or MATCH_CANCELED (Cancel) before
  the cabinet gives up. A 4-human room still wins whenever possible. Config default VsCpu / 18 s.
- CpuPartnerCancelSeconds (default 5, 0 = off): with NoCpuPartner a 2v2 entry with a CPU partner ("N") is never
  placed; it now gets MATCH_CANCELED after 5 s instead of sitting out the 150 s cabinet timeout (13:40-13:46 PT).
- server.json and tools/vps/server.vps.json: VsCpu, 18, 5.
- 15 new unit tests (ContinuePairTests).

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
