From 9c73f17e698af624772e34fa63dba9da0568d83f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:24:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 35/52] Matchmaker: duo vs 2 CPU stand-ins after 12s (AnyDuo
 scope), place CPU-partner teams in full rooms

- ContinuePairScope AnyDuo (default): any 2-human team entry gets the VsCpu room, not only recent
  same-side teammates (14:15 PT retest: the pair had been opponents; history lost on restart)
- VsCpu builds humans-vs-2-stand-ins (played by the game) instead of the bare lone-team room
  (not played); no free stand-in id -> MATCH_CANCELED on the same poll
- ContinuePairSeconds 12 (cabinet cancels itself at ~28-34s; polls at +3s then ~15s)
- PlaceCpuPartnerTeams (config default true): a human + own-CPU-partner team entry may be placed in a
  full room vs two humans (14:21 PT: cab 1 looped CPU-partner entries, 3 solos never matched);
  never short-handed, all-human rooms ranked first, fast cancel skipped while on

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
