From 17990783204cfe3b5e3f1e682ff63d3e99702b54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:54:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 36/52] Matchmaker: two lone solos vs 2 CPU stand-ins after
 12s, waiting first for a running CPU room's players

22:32-22:47Z retest: after each 4-human room the winners continue as a duo (CPU room via ContinuePair), while
for the losers a loss ends the play even on free play (save_charge ConsectiveWin=0); losers re-enter after an
automatic card re-read (about +60 s), as two solos 33-67 s after the duo, and sat in a NOCPU hold until the
150 s timeout, repeatedly.

- SoloPairVsCpuSeconds (config default 12): exactly two all-human solos in the world's queue, both waited 12 s ->
  teammates (g0) vs two CPU stand-ins, the shape the game played 01:23 PT. A 4-human room always wins.
- SoloPairReturnWaitSeconds (config default 270): while a humans-vs-CPU room of the same world (not their own)
  started < 270 s ago, the solos wait for its players instead (winners return as a duo ~130 s, losers as solos
  ~235-250 s after it), so all four regroup.
- 12 new tests (372 total).

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
