From ca3591127cf6eefdfbaa75b23c66047a49fc95dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:45:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 38/52] Matchmaker: class/free solo-team world links for the
 regroup wait, experimental cross-world team room

Class match test 15:34-15:41 PT: the winners continued as a class-team duo (world 14) and got the
ContinuePair CPU room; the losers came back as class-solo solos (world 13) after the automatic card re-read.
The SoloPairReturnWait check compared world ids exactly, so the solos took their own CPU room at +12 s.

- SoloPairReturnWait now also counts a CPU room in the linked solo/team world (13/14, 18/19, 15/16, 6/7,
  26/27), so the solos wait and regroup with the CPU-room players when those come back as solos.
- CrossWorldTeamRooms (EXPERIMENTAL, default false, untested with the game): a lone class-team/free-team duo
  plus exactly two solos waiting in the linked solo world get one 4-human room (duo g0, solos g1), for the
  case where the duo wins its CPU match and continues as a team again.
- 6 new tests (378 total).

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
