From 3bd275c230781b55e64a42ebcebf0b65d430fc89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:02:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 39/52] Solo pair vs CPU: off by default (cabs stuck after it),
 add a 4-human regroup guard

Mix test 15:44-15:58 PT on ff9ec8b: room 7 (cabs 2+4, two solo entries teamed vs 2 CPU
stand-ins) saved results at 15:57:02 and neither cab sent another request; class room 3
(15:39:28, same shape) never reported a result, and the 01:23 PT test cabs were silent
after 01:26:22. Continued duos vs CPU always carried on. SoloPairVsCpuSeconds now
defaults to 0, so solos hold under NoCpuPartner until four humans meet (15:51:17).

If it is re-enabled, SoloPairRegroupSeconds (75) keeps two solos waiting while the other
players of their last 4-human room have not searched again (15:53:51 winners came back
as two solos and got CPUs at 15:54:03; the losers arrived 15:54:39/48).

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
