From e52346f28cf943caf5fb2ed4a178a0c463f12bde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:08:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 40/52] Matchmaker: pair-keep-searching test (no CPU room for
 waiting duos)

Official cabinets keep a searching pair queued and let the game start a
waiting practice fight that a real match can interrupt. Ours currently
answers a lone duo with a CPU room after 12s (ContinuePairMode=VsCpu),
which ends the search so later cabs cannot join.

PairNeverCpu (or PairCpuFallbackSeconds=0) holds every all-human duo,
including a ContinuePair, until 4 humans meet or the cabinet times out
or cancels. Off in the normal config; on in
tools/vps/server.vps.pair-keep-searching.json. Everything else is
unchanged (linked-world wait, regroup 75s, SoloPairVsCpu off,
CrossWorldTeamRooms off).

PAIR-SEARCH log lines record each pair entry, poll (answer, gap, whether
it passed the ~30s pair timer), cancel, stale drop, and any unusual MMS
method from that cabinet.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
