From 869f5299d0204d38439265203fc268e215dbcd7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:44:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 41/52] Matchmaker: quarantine cancelled pair nodes until a
 clean restart

12:19-12:23 AM PT Nov 16: a searching duo (PCB_03 node 1258, partner 1260)
hit the ~30 s in-game pair timer, the leader sent CancelMatching (apply=3),
both cabs black-screened, then PCB_03 re-entered as a mix solo on the same
node 1258 (apply=4, no IssueNodeId) and was placed in a 4-solo room with
cabs that had fresh nodes. The other three got LiveMonitor 21-01 during
loading.

After CancelMatching, or a stale / matching-timeout drop, of an all-human
duo, those node ids and cabinet serials are kept out of human rooms. A
quarantined re-entry is answered WAIT (Success, empty room): that is the
game's normal keep-polling reply, so the dirty cab is never placed with
others. MATCH_CANCELED stays reserved for a search that has actually ended.

Quarantine lifts when the cab enters with a new node id (IssueNodeId after
a clean restart) or after PairCancelQuarantineSeconds (default 180; 0 = off;
negative = until a new node only). QUARANTINE add/hold/clear lines are
logged. 11 new tests (410 total).

MthdSaveFailedBattleLogOn already has a no-op Success stub in this repo
(PostMatchStubCommandHandler) that logs room, pilots and fault flags.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
