+## Pair search, class match, and cabinet tests (2026-11-16)
+
+Cabinet tests on 2026-11-15 and 2026-11-16 (four cabinets, one Live Monitor, shared VPS matchmaker; times Pacific Time).
+A longer plain-language write-up, including how official Japanese cabinets differ, is in the
+[exvs2-matchmaking](https://github.com/ServerOmega/exvs2-matchmaking) docs:
+[docs/MATCHMAKING-BEHAVIOUR.md](https://github.com/ServerOmega/exvs2-matchmaking/blob/prerelease/pair-cancel-guard/docs/MATCHMAKING-BEHAVIOUR.md)
+and [docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md](https://github.com/ServerOmega/exvs2-matchmaking/blob/prerelease/pair-cancel-guard/docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md).
+Do not publish a VPS public IP; use `<VPS_IP>`.
+
+### Free-play / GAME OVER
+These cabinets are free-play. After a loss the card is often re-read automatically about 45–60 s later and the
+player can search again. Official 1-credit play is not like that: a loss is GAME OVER and needs another credit.
+Winners who continue as a pair usually re-enter the queue well before the losers are back.
+
+### The in-game ~30 s pair timer
+A searching pair that stays on a bare "finding opponents" screen is cancelled by **the game**, not the server,
+after about 30 seconds. The cabinet then shows a partner-lost / "stick with a CPU?" prompt. If the two cabinets
+answer that prompt differently, both can sit on a black screen for around two minutes.
+
+### Rooms are final once sent
+When CheckMatching returns a room, that room is finished. The server cannot later merge two 1v1 groups into one
+2v2, or pull new humans into an already-sent CPU room. Official Infinite Boost documentation does not describe
+that kind of mid-search merge either. Mix Match can put a pair and two solos in one room **at matching time**;
+that is not combining two rooms that already started.
+
+### ContinuePair VsCpu at 18 s
+`ContinuePairMode=VsCpu` (default) sends a lone all-human pair a room against two CPU stand-ins after
+`ContinuePairSeconds`. The shipped default is **18 s**, the original value from the continue-pair fix.
+18 is under the game's ~30 s timer, so the CPU room arrives before the partner-lost prompt. **Do not set this
+to 30**: that races the in-game timer and can bring the black screen back. 12 s was tried later so the answer
+would be ready with more margin before the second CheckMatching poll (the pair leader polls at about 3 s, then
+every 15 s). 18 s was restored after the 2026-11-16 tests, and a pair that waited with only one other cabinet
+searching did get the CPU room at 18 s with no prompt.
+
+### Solo pair vs CPU (off)
+`SoloPairVsCpuSeconds` could send two leftover solos versus CPUs after a short wait. In testing this froze
+cabinets, so it is **off by default** (0). Leave it off.
+
+### Class Match solo / team split
+Class Match solo (world **13**) and Class Match team (world **14**) are separate queues, matching official
+Class Match G (solo and team have separate class tracks). The server links those worlds (and free-solo 18 /
+free-team 19) for some regroup waiting, but a class pair and two class solos still cannot share one class room
+unless `CrossWorldTeamRooms` is on. That option is **experimental, off, and untested with the game**.
+Workaround: use **Mix Match** for a night of pairs and solos together, or have the two solos also pair up so
+both teams are in the team queue.
+
+### PairNeverCpu test (off)
+`PairNeverCpu` (and `PairCpuFallbackSeconds=0`) was a test: never answer a waiting pair with a CPU room, and
+keep them in the queue, in the hope they could practice and still be matched. Cabinet test 2026-11-15 evening:
+the server kept the pair waiting, but at about 30 s the **game** cancelled the search and showed the
+partner-lost prompt. Because the two cabinets answered differently, both went to a black screen. The unpatched
+game does **not** practice-and-keep-search. The flag is off in this build. Official cabinets avoid a long idle
+search by starting waiting Practice while the search continues; this server cannot do that by itself.
+
+### Optional game change (last resort, not in this build)
+There is research into a small game-side change that would raise the in-game pair-search timeout (about 30 s)
+toward the general matching timeout (about 150 s), so a pair could stay in search longer and closer to official
+waiting Practice. That work is a last resort, is not part of this pre-release, and this document does not include
+patch bytes or offsets.
+
+### Pair-cancel quarantine
+After a pair cancels (or is dropped stale / on timeout), `PairCancelQuarantineSeconds` (default 180) holds those
+node ids and cabinet serials out of new human rooms. A quarantined re-entry is answered WAIT (the normal
+keep-polling reply), never placed. The hold lifts when the cabinet enters with a **new node id** (IssueNodeId
+after a clean restart / title-screen card swipe) or when the timer expires. This blocks the 21-01 case where a
+half-reset cab (same node, no fresh IssueNodeId) joined a room with cabs that had come back cleanly.
+
+### 21-01 disconnects
+Live Monitor error 21-01 means the cabinets lost the LM or could not finish loading a match. Causes seen in
+these tests:
+
+* The matchmaker host restarted (a VPS deploy). Every cab drops for the downtime.
+* The Live Monitor process was closed (or had already failed its card-server check). Searching cabs notice first;
+  cabs still in a CPU match notice when that match ends.
+* A half-reset cab joining a room with freshly restarted cabs (the case the quarantine is meant to stop).
+
+The game does not retry its card-server check. Start the **card servers first**, then the LM and the cabinets.
+If the LM and cabs start while the card servers are down, they fail that check and never talk to the card
+servers until they are closed and started again.
+
+Outside internet hosts also send junk traffic at the VPS STUN / match ports. The same noise was present during
+matches that completed normally, so it was not the cause of the 21-01s.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
+  (`BindMatchNodesToSourceIp` limits Check/Cancel to the IP that entered, but is not a login.)
 * Malformed protobuf bodies on `/match` get HTTP 500 from the model binder (the real cabinet never sends them).
 * Hole-punch / P2P packet format unknown; real battles need reachable UDP (public IP/UPnP or a shared VPN).
 * Mode→world mapping, class ids (1–4) and the hour-based schedule are inferred, not observed.
 * `Grade1Solo/Team`, promotion matches, Extreme ladder (`LoadRankMatch`) untouched.
 * Hand-written migration has no Designer file (EF applies it; snapshot updated).
-* Matchmaker state is in memory; restart drops waiting players (node ids persist, their polls get MATCH_CANCELED).
+* Matchmaker state is in memory; restart drops waiting players (node ids persist, their polls get MATCH_CANCELED)
+  and running cabinets can show Live Monitor 21-01 while the process is down.
 * A room is never refilled or torn down when a member drops after the match: the protocol has no message for it.
+  Rooms are also final once sent (no later 1v1-to-2v2 merge).
 * Ranked results are saved per card (`SaveVsmOnResult`); a side that never reports simply records nothing.
-* Online tag / recruit: the CheckMatching shape the game expects for worlds 5/21/22 (2 clients, both group 0) is a
-  guess; `tag_status` meaning unknown; recruit leader rule unknown; tags only within one card server (ids collide
-  across servers). Untested in the real game.
+* A pair that loses to CPUs and searches again can still get the in-game partner-lost prompt and a black screen
+  (under investigation; the quarantine stops a bad follow-up room, it does not remove the prompt).
+* Class Match keeps solo (world 13) and team (world 14) in separate queues; a class pair cannot match two class
+  solos with `CrossWorldTeamRooms` off.
+* Online tag across card servers and friend requests are implemented and were tested (see sections above);
+  partner recruit (worlds 21/22) is less tested. `tag_status` must be 1 for the in-game list to be selectable.
+
 
 ## Hosting the matchmaker on a VPS
 See [tools/vps/README.md](tools/vps/README.md): `tools/vps/deploy.sh` builds a committed ref for linux-x64 and runs it
